    <div hidden>
      <div data-diag="wifi"><b>The Wi-Fi drops in some rooms</b><p><span>Might mean:</span> access points in the wrong spots, interference, or tired equipment.</p><p><span>We'd check:</span> coverage room by room and how the access points are set up.</p></div>
      <div data-diag="slow"><b>PCs feel slower than they should</b><p><span>Might mean:</span> missing updates, a failing drive, or too much starting up at login.</p><p><span>We'd check:</span> update status, drive health and what runs when the PC starts.</p></div>
      <div data-diag="backups"><b>Nobody's sure the backups work</b><p><span>Might mean:</span> backups that quietly stopped, or never covered the files that matter.</p><p><span>We'd check:</span> when they last ran, what they cover, and whether a restore actually works.</p></div>
      <div data-diag="access"><b>A former employee might still have access</b><p><span>Might mean:</span> accounts that were never switched off when someone left.</p><p><span>We'd check:</span> every account, who it belongs to and what it can reach.</p></div>
      <div data-diag="phish"><b>Strange pop-ups, or emails "from us" we didn't send</b><p><span>Might mean:</span> an email account someone else has signed in to, or unwanted software on a PC.</p><p><span>We'd check:</span> the affected accounts and machines, and recent sign-ins.</p></div>
      <div data-diag="printer"><b>The printer and the internet fight every morning</b><p><span>Might mean:</span> two devices trying to use the same network address, or a router that needs attention.</p><p><span>We'd check:</span> how devices get their addresses and how the router is set up.</p></div>
      <div data-diag="unknown"><b>Nobody knows what's plugged into the network</b><p><span>Might mean:</span> nothing is wrong yet. It just means nobody has a list.</p><p><span>We'd check:</span> everything that's connected, then write it down for you.</p></div>
